# These lines hold Supabase's publishable key (sb_publishable_…). It is made for browsers, is already served publicly
# at halom.io/mana/config.js, and row-level security guards the data, so gitleaks' generic-api-key rule is a false
# positive here. Secret keys (sb_secret_…, service_role) must never be in this repository.
# The entries are line numbers: after editing CONTRACT.md or config.js, run `gitleaks detect --no-git --source .` and
# move them to the new lines. Every config file (config.js, config/demo.js: the demo database `mana`'s publishable key)
# keeps its key on line 4, so `config.js:generic-api-key:4` also covers _site/config.js; tools/check-config.mjs checks
# that each entry here still points at a publishable key.
config.js:generic-api-key:4
config/demo.js:generic-api-key:4
CONTRACT.md:generic-api-key:45
CONTRACT.md:generic-api-key:195
